{% set local_problem %}
<p>Athens' age is one of its greatest assets — historic character, established neighborhoods, mature trees, homes with stories to tell. But that age comes with maintenance challenges. Fascia boards that have been exposed to Alabama's humidity for 40, 50, or 60+ years don't last forever, especially when gutters start failing and water begins running where it shouldn't.</p>

<p>We see this constantly throughout Athens: homeowners call about new gutters, but when we inspect their homes, we find fascia that's soft, water-stained, or visibly rotting behind the existing gutters. The damage often started years ago when gutters began leaking or overflowing, sending water behind them to soak into the wood. Alabama's humidity doesn't let that wood dry out — it stays damp, creating perfect conditions for rot, mold, and wood-destroying insects.</p>

<p>The neighborhoods around Athens State University, near downtown, and throughout central Athens are particularly affected. These areas have some of the oldest housing stock in Limestone County, with original fascia boards that have seen decades of Alabama weather. Even homes that look well-maintained from the street often have hidden fascia damage waiting behind their gutters.</p>

<p>Installing new gutters on rotted wood is pointless — they won't stay securely attached, and the underlying damage will continue spreading. The only real solution is to address the fascia first, then install gutters that will actually last.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with a thorough inspection, checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you exactly what we find and explain what needs repair — no hidden damage, no surprise charges later.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we carefully remove existing gutters, cut out the rotted wood back to solid material, and install new fascia boards. We use quality primed lumber or composite materials specifically designed for exterior exposure in humid climates like Alabama's — materials that will hold up to decades of Athens weather.</p>

<p>Everything is properly sealed, caulked, and prepared for new gutter installation. Then we install your new seamless gutters on the fresh fascia — properly attached with appropriate hangers, properly sloped for drainage, and designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot in the first place.</p>

<p>You get a complete solution from one contractor: carpentry, gutters, and the peace of mind that comes from knowing the job was done right.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia and installing gutters throughout Athens and Limestone County for over 20 years. We understand that these two jobs are inseparable — you can't have reliable gutters without solid fascia to mount them on, and you can't protect fascia without properly functioning gutters to keep water away from it.</p>

<p>Our crews handle both carpentry and gutter installation, which means better coordination, cleaner work, and a single point of accountability. We've worked on Athens homes of every era — from historic downtown residences to mid-century neighborhoods to modern construction — and we understand the specific challenges each presents.</p>
{% endset %}
